<section class="problem">

<div class="card">

<h3>

The Problem

</h3>

<p>

A raw list of companies is not a pipeline.

Manual list-building gives you names with zero context — no fit signal, no sense of who deserves a rep's time, and no personalization beyond a mail-merged first name.

</p>

<ul>

<li>No fit scoring</li>

<li>Personalization doesn't scale</li>

<li>Signals live in five different tabs</li>

<li>One channel, one message, no nuance</li>

</ul>

</div>

<div class="card">

<h3>

The Solution

</h3>

<p>

Outbound Intelligence Engine treats every lead as a decision, not a row.

Each company is enriched, scored against a weighted ICP model, researched for a live signal, and turned into three distinct, channel-appropriate messages — before a single email goes out.

</p>

<ul>

<li>Weighted ICP scoring</li>

<li>Live signal research via Claygent</li>

<li>Three tailored messages per lead</li>

<li>Tier-gated, human-approved sending</li>

</ul>

</div>

</section>
